course: dictionary
lesson: 5832
title: Maize and corn: same plant, different names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Words can have different names in different places. «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.» Maize is a tall plant with yellow seeds called kernels, which grow on large cobs.
explain: Context clues can show you what a word means. «Maize, or corn, is a grass too.» The words «or corn» tell you that maize and corn are two names for the same plant.
explain: Maize has a second meaning as well: the seeds of the plant, which people eat or give to animals. Ask yourself whether the sentence is talking about the growing plant or the seeds. The rest of the sentence will tell you which.
fact: Maize is a tall cereal plant with yellow seeds called kernels, which grow on large cobs.
fact: Maize can also mean the seeds of that plant, used as food or fed to animals.
fact: British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand English often say "maize"; Americans and Canadians say "corn".
fact: Maize came from teosinte, a wild grass of Mexico, after farmers kept seed from their best plants for thousands of years.
fact: Foods made from maize include popcorn, cornflakes, tortillas, polenta and corn on the cob.
exercise: «Maize, or corn, is a grass too.» What do the words «or corn» tell you? | They show that maize is a kind of animal | They say the grass has died | They say maize is only grown in winter | *They show that maize and corn are two names for the same plant
exercise: Which food is made from maize? | Orange juice | *Tortillas | Cheese
exercise: Teosinte is the wild grass that maize came from. Which country is it a wild grass of? | Ethiopia | Australia | *Mexico | Ireland
test: In Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, which word is often used for this crop? | Corn | Kernel | *Maize | Teosinte
test: «Rice, wheat and maize are the most important crops in the world.» Which crop came from the Middle East? | Potatoes | Chilli | Maize | *Wheat
exam: Which sentence uses maize to mean the seeds, not the plant? | Teosinte is a wild grass of Mexico | Maize is a tall plant with yellow cobs | Maize grows best in a warm field | *Farmers feed maize to their animals
